## The 4 structural problems
1. **Subprocessor list = 3 representations, 2 departments, out of sync.** Standalone list (2026-04-28, InfoSec) vs Appendix B (2026-02-25, embedded in a customer's DPA) vs VENDOR MASTER SHEET. The standalone list is **newer** than the "authoritative" Appendix B.
2. **Templates ≠ latest.** The SLA "template" is the retired 90%; the true canonical 99% sits in a customer folder. A draft update is floating separately.
3. **DPA duplication.** Hosting DPA exists in InfoSec (`2. DPA`), in Sales&CS templates (2 variants), and per-customer. Marketplace DPA "template" is in Sales&CS but the authoritative copy is in a customer folder.
4. **No declared source-of-truth pointer** linking the two departments' copies.

