## Alternatives

### Alt 1 — Consolidate everything under InfoSec (governance-led)
Move canonical templates + SLA + DPAs into `05 - InfoSec` alongside Vendor Management.
- ✅ Governance, versioning discipline, VENDOR MASTER SHEET, auditor evidence already here.
- ❌ SLA/DPA templates are commercial artifacts the sales team edits daily; readme says don't add folders.

### Alt 2 — Consolidate everything under Sales & CS / Contracts & Agreements (commercial-led)
Make `01 - Customer agreement Templates` the canonical home for all master templates + the subprocessor list.
- ✅ Templates + sales workflow already here.
- ❌ Splits governance: master sheet, archive, signed-DPA store, auditor evidence all live in InfoSec.

### Alt 3 — Split by document *nature* (RECOMMENDED) — no migration
Each artifact gets ONE owning home by what it is; both existing homes are already correct:
- **Subprocessor lists (all variants) + VENDOR MASTER SHEET** → stay in `InfoSec / 05 - Vendor Management / 00 - PII Sub-processor Management`. Make this THE single list; reconcile the standalone-vs-Appendix-B split so the **DPA references the list** (or Appendix B is generated from it) instead of restating it.
- **Canonical templates** (Main Agreement, Terms, SLA, both DPA templates, Marketplace Order) → stay in `Sales & CS / 01 - Customer agreement Templates`, but fix in place: replace the 90% SLA with the canonical 99%, promote the 2026-05-29 draft to "current," retire duplicates to `old/`.
- **Executed/signed per-customer docs** → stay in `Sales & CS / 00 - Customer agreements / <Customer>`.
- **Add ONE "Contract Source of Truth" index** — a short Google Doc (or a tab on the VENDOR MASTER SHEET) listing the canonical SLA / Marketplace DPA / Hosting DPA / subprocessor list with live links + "last updated." This is the cheap consolidation: a map, not a move.
- ✅ Sustainable, zero risky migration, no broken links/Vanta refs, respects the readme. If a physical move is ever wanted, the index becomes the move checklist.
- ❌ Still two physical homes (mitigated by the index + fixing staleness).

### Alt 4 — New top-level "Legal & Contracts" home
Move everything into a brand-new dedicated top-level folder.
- ✅ One clean home.
- ❌ Heavy migration, breaks links + Vanta/auditor refs, violates the InfoSec readme, splits governance from ISMS context. **Not recommended.**

